<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Singapore</h1><p class="st-meta">1965 CE – present · capital Singapore</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Island city-state that became independent in 1965 and turned itself into one of the world's richest trading and financial hubs.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After two years in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/malaysia">Malaysia</a>, disputes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lee-kuan-yew">Lee Kuan Yew's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-action-party">People's Action Party</a> and the federal government over racial politics led to Singapore's separation. On 9 August 1965 it became an independent republic, small, without natural resources and dependent on its port.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-action-party">People's Action Party</a> has governed without interruption, combining elections with tight control of the press and opposition. The state attracted foreign manufacturers, built public housing for most citizens through the Housing and Development Board, and fostered a multiracial identity with English, Malay, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandarin-chinese">Mandarin</a> and Tamil as official languages. Its port and airport became among the busiest in the world.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goh-chok-tong">Goh Chok Tong</a> from 1990 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lee-hsien-loong">Lee Hsien Loong</a> from 2004 Singapore became a centre of finance and technology. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lawrence-wong">Lawrence Wong</a> became prime minister in 2024, the fourth since independence.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/singapore.jpg" alt="Singapore" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Government of Singapore Vector: Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Singapore.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1965 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Singapore</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Lee Kuan Yew, Goh Chok Tong, Lee Hsien Loong</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism, Christianity, Sunni Islam, Taoism, Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Malay, Mandarin, Tamil</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/singapore">Singapore</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Singapore</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1996&amp;focus=singapore" aria-label="Singapore on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7563 2129 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Singapore lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7883 2385L7823 2316M7883 2385L7883 2385"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7823 2316h0M7883 2385h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7883 2385h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7883 2385h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Singapore. <a href="/atlas?year=1996&amp;focus=singapore">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
